Upstream PR: https://github.com/vyperlang/vyper/pull/5280
Status: merged 2026-10-02 (f89b81f9b85533791c8191bbdf1fa1a08bde0ffe)

Reject an assignment, augmented-assignment, append or pop target whose
subscript base passes through a dynamic-array element while its index can
write a variable that base reads, or makes a risky call.

Adapted to this pin: the pin already has the overlap helpers
(_subscript_read_write_overlap, _subscript_base_length_can_stale and the
risky-call walk) and already rejects assignment and augmented-assignment
targets, which _get_target_ptr lowers with as_ptr=True. Only upstream's
hunk is kept: append and pop lower their array with as_ptr=True, so they
reject too instead of writing into a snapshot of the base. Upstream's
darray_indices argument is not in the pin and is left out.

